Anatomy of a CSS Rule
---------------------
A CSS rule is made up of three parts:

selector {
    property: value;
}

1) Selector
   - Tells which HTML element you want to style
   - Example: p, h1, .className, #idName

2) Property
   - The characteristic you want to change
   - Example: color, font-size, background, margin

3) Value
   - The setting you want to apply to the property
   - Example: red, 20px, center, blue

Full Example:

p {
    color: blue;
    font-size: 16px;
}

Selector: p
Properties: color, font-size
Values: blue, 16px
